    "rationale": "Present risk is critical in the absence of controls because an untrusted supplier invoice can drive bank-detail updates and irreversible payment scheduling under broad ERP credentials. Residual risk is high because the only declared preventive control is a human approval gate that is wired to the sensitive capabilities, but it is a model-summary gate at high review volume, so rubric step 2 reduces critical by one tier and the summary framing prevents stronger credit. Forecast returns to critical if model upgrades, autonomy increases, the gate is removed, or longer task horizons further erode the dependent aspects of summary approval. The control whose decay moves the forecast most is ctl.clerk_approval."
  },
